<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hermanus Steyn</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1743–<a href="/years/1804">1804</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hermanus Steyn was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burghers">burgher</a> of the Swellendam district of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-colony">Cape Colony</a>. In June 1795, after the settlers expelled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a>'s landdrost, he was chosen president of their assembly of national representatives in the short-lived Swellendam Republic. The republic submitted to British rule after the British occupied the Cape later that year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hermanus-steyn.jpg" alt="Hermanus Steyn" width="320" height="352" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:President_Hermanus_Steyn.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
